# Reviewed findings baseline for the conformance corpus, at the PIN rev.
# One data line per expected finding at gating confidence (deny/confirmed):
#   <crate>\t<code>\t<kernel>\t<confidence>
# The runner fails on any EXTRA finding (a false positive) and on any
# MISSING line (a detection regression). Warning-confidence findings are
# reported but not baselined: the release gate is zero FP at default
# confidence.
#
# conformance-constant_index_from_end/write_last deliberately takes
# `&mut [u32]` (upstream's last-element addressing test). Upstream's own
# safety model says to treat such a kernel as unsafe, so RC003 here is a
# reviewed true positive, not an FP.
conformance_constant_index_from_end	RC003	write_last	deny

# conformance_unroll_bounds_check (all seven kernels) takes `arr: &mut [u32]`
# as a `#[kernel]` parameter. The crate is upstream's regression corpus for a
# bounds-check bug in the `#[unroll]` MIR transform -- the slice is there to
# be indexed out of range on purpose (`arr[999] = 7`), not because anyone
# should write a kernel that way. RC003 is correct on every one of them:
# `&mut [T]` is one exclusive reference handed to every thread, and upstream's
# own safety model says the same. Reviewed true positives, not FPs.
conformance_unroll_bounds_check	RC003	control	deny
conformance_unroll_bounds_check	RC003	full_after	deny
conformance_unroll_bounds_check	RC003	full_before	deny
conformance_unroll_bounds_check	RC003	full_inside	deny
conformance_unroll_bounds_check	RC003	partial_after	deny
conformance_unroll_bounds_check	RC003	partial_before	deny
conformance_unroll_bounds_check	RC003	partial_inside	deny
